data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:32:31.480909+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_ee85678f9c3a", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this carefully. I'm an orchestrator in an EarthScope GNSS agent. The user is asking me to:\n\n1. Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles\n2. Stage its time-series CSV\n3. Profile it\n4. Create a displacement time-series plot\n\nThis is a multi-step task that requires orchestration through the pipeline:\n- First, I need to resolve \"Los Angeles\" to coordinates \u2192 `geospatial`\n- Then discover stations near LA and stage the nearest one \u2192 `data`\n- Then profile the staged CSV \u2192 `analysis`\n- Then create a visualization \u2192 `visualization`\n- Finally synthesize the answer \u2192 `synthesis`\n\nAccording to the instructions:\n- I should NOT do the work myself\n- I have child experts with tools\n- I must delegate ONE child at a time\n- Each child returns typed evidence in `workflow_state`\n- I only have NO tools and NO grounded knowledge\n- I must route based on what the request actually asks for\n\nThe request asks to:\n1. Find + stage a station (discovery + staging)\n2. Profile it (analysis)\n3. Plot it (visualization)\n\nSo the pipeline should be: `geospatial` \u2192 `data` \u2192 `analysis` \u2192 `visualization` \u2192 `synthesis`\n\nLet me start with `geospatial` since the request names a place (\"Los Angeles\") but doesn't provide explicit coordinates.\n\nMy reasoning should explain why I'm delegating to geospatial first.\n\nMy answer field should be EMPTY at this stage because I have no evidence yet. According to the instructions: \"If you have done no delegation yet, you have no evidence yet \u2014 do not finish.\"\n\nMy workflow_state should be initialized to track the pipeline state. I should include information about what stage we're at.\n\nMy next_expert should be `geospatial`.\n\nMy next_task should be specific: resolve Los Angeles to coordinates and a region definition.\n\nLet me construct the response:\nThe user wants a complete workflow: converting the place name to coordinates, finding and staging the nearest station, analyzing the data, and generating a visualization. I'll need to move through geospatial resolution first, then data discovery and staging, followed by profiling and visualization work. Since \"Los Angeles\" is a location name rather than coordinates, I should start by delegating to geospatial to establish the region.\n\n```\n"}, "replay": true}

