ved\n\nFor the radius, I can calculate it from the bounding box dimensions. The bbox spans approximately 0.5 degrees longitude and 0.68 degrees latitude, which translates to roughly 40-50 km at this latitude. I'll use this to determine an appropriate radius value for the geospatial region. The system prompt specifies I should choose a conservative regional-analysis radius and record it in warnings as an assumed default. For Los Angeles County, 50 km is a standard choice that balances capturing the administrative area without being overly broad. I'll use that value and note it as an assumption.\n\nI have the geocoding result with precise coordinates and bounding box from Nominatim, so I can now complete the task and format the geospatial output. The finish tool signals that all necessary information is available for extraction. I have the geocoding result for Los Angeles from OpenStreetMap Nominatim with coordinates (34.0536909, -118.242766) and a bounding box for the administrative area. The importance score of 0.84 gives me confidence in this result. Since no explicit radius was specified, I'll apply a default 50 km regional analysis radius and note this assumption. Now I'm ready to call finish to signal that all necessary information for the outputs is available. I have the geocoding result for Los Angeles from OpenStreetMap and can now signal completion. The workflow_state extraction happens implicitly when the finish tool is called\u2014the agent framework will compile the geospatial data from the trajectory into the required JSON format. My next step is to call finish with empty arguments. I've resolved the location to center coordinates (34.0536909, -118.242766) with a strong confidence score of 0.84. Since no specific radius was provided, I'm applying a 50 km regional analysis radius as a conservative default and will note this assumption. The geospatial region object is ready to be compiled with all necessary parameters."}}

