ng results\u2014Los Angeles at 34.0537\u00b0N, 118.2428\u00b0W with an administrative boundary spanning the county. I'll use the bounding box coordinates to calculate an appropriate radius and set confidence to high given the 0.84 importance score and direct OSM match. The workflow state captures the resolved region with center coordinates derived from the geocode result, the bounding box from the administrative boundary, and high confidence based on the direct match quality. min_lat, max_lon, max_lat]. For the radius, since no specific distance was mentioned in the request, I need to select a conservative default. The bbox spans roughly 46 km longitudinally and 75 km latitudinally, so I'll set the radius to 50 km as an appropriate regional search radius and document this assumption in warnings. The confidence level should be \"high\" given the 0.84 importance score and administrative-level match. The provenance is osm_nominatim, and I need to include a warning noting the assumed default radius. 34.0536909,\n    \"center_lon\": -118.242766,\n    \"radius_km\": 50,\n    \"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306],\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\",\n    \"warnings\": [\"Default search radius of 50 km assumed; no explicit radius was specified in the request.\"]\n  },\n  \"temporal\": null,\n  \"thematic\": null\n}\n```\n\nThe response structure now has the geospatial resolution complete with the geocoded Los Angeles location, its bounding box from the nominatim result, and a note about the assumed radius since the user didn't specify one. The workflow state carries forward the prior acquisition and temporal/thematic fields as null while populating the geospatial section with the resolved region data. I need to clarify something: the text you've provided appears to be output formatting instructions and schema documentation, not thinking that needs to be rewritten.\n\nCould you please provide the actual thinking content that you'd like me to rewrite? I'm looking for Claude's internal reasoning or thought process that needs to be condensed and reformatted according to the guidelines you've outlined.\n\nOnce you share the thinking content, I'll rewrite it concisely while maintaining fidelity to the original reasoning and following all the guidelines you've specified."}}

