data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:34:21.458978+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_c3d9a1e653c5", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me break down what's happening here:\n\n1. I'm an orchestrator expert in a multi-turn workflow system\n2. The user's original request is: \"Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles, stage its time-series CSV, profile it, and create a displacement time-series plot.\"\n3. The geospatial child has already completed and returned:\n   - region_name: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n   - center_lat: 34.0536909\n   - center_lon: -118.242766\n   - radius_km: 50\n   - confidence: high\n   - provenance: osm_nominatim\n\n4. Current workflow_state shows:\n   - geospatial: resolved \u2713\n   - acquisition: None (not yet staged)\n   - profile: None (not yet profiled)\n   - visualization: None (not yet visualized)\n   - pipeline_stage: geospatial_resolved\n\n5. The request summary identifies requirements:\n   - station_discovery\n   - time_series_staging\n   - profiling\n   - visualization\n\n6. Already run: ['geospatial']\n7. Not yet run: ['analysis', 'data', 'synthesis', 'visualization']\n\nAccording to the instructions:\n- The user asks to FIND, STAGE, PROFILE, and PLOT\n- This means: geospatial \u2192 data (discover + stage) \u2192 analysis (profile) \u2192 visualization (plot) \u2192 synthesis (final answer)\n- The request is for the full study: find stations \u2192 stage data \u2192 profile \u2192 plot\n- I should NOT skip any steps\n- I should route to ONE child at a time and advance based on their evidence\n\nNext step: Route to `data` expert\n- Task: Discover the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles (center: 34.0536909, -118.242766, radius: 50 km), rank candidates by distance, and stage the time-series CSV for the nearest station.\n- The data expert will identify available stations within the region, select the closest one, retrieve and stage its time-series CSV, then return the acquisition status and staged file path to update workflow_state.\n\nThe geospatial expert has pinpointed Los Angeles with specific coordinates and a 50 km radius. The user wants to find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station, stage its data, analyze it, and generate a displacement visualization. I need to hand off to the data expert to query for stations in that area, sort by distance, and prepare the CSV for the nearest one with complete records. Once that's staged, the workflow will move through profiling and plotting before final synthesis."}}

