urce": "live"}, "agent_id": "data", "text": "data -> ndp_dataset_discovery", "parent_agent": "data", "child_agent": "ndp_dataset_discovery", "stage": "delegate.started", "thought": "The geospatial expert has already resolved Los Angeles to a precise center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W) with a 50 km radius. The `acquisition` field is currently `\"None\"`, meaning the data branch has not yet started.\n\nTo complete the user's request, I must orchestrate the three-stage pipeline in strict order:\n\n1. **First**: `ndp_dataset_discovery` searches NDP and stages the EarthScope station metadata catalog CSV (returns `acquisition.metadata_path`)\n2. **Then**: `earthscope_station_catalog` spatially filters and ranks nearby stations from that catalog (returns ranked `station_ids`)\n3. **Finally**: `ndp_resource_resolver` stages the nearest ranked station's time-series CSV (returns `acquisition.status=staged` with `acquisition.local_path`)\n\nI have no tools of my own and no grounded knowledge of available datasets, station locations, or paths. Only my children's tool calls produce real evidence. This is a routing turn\u2014I delegate to the first child and forward the already-resolved geospatial state without inventing any acquisition, catalog, or resource_candidate facts.", "status": "running"}}, "replay": true}

