data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:34:53.767762+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_33ca2a064068", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me carefully parse the instructions here. The user is asking me to act as an agent following a very specific protocol with THREE tool calls:\n\n1. **STEP 1**: Search for the EarthScope station metadata catalog using `ndp_search_datasets` with EXACT arguments:\n   - `search_terms: [\"earthscope\", \"converted\"]`\n   - `limit: 10`\n   - No `search_term` (singular), no `filter_list`, no `resource_format`, no `server`\n\n2. **STEP 2**: Stage the CSV catalog found in step 1 using `ndp_stage_resource` with:\n   - `url`: The exact URL from step 1's result\n   - `output_dir`: The Active workspace root (which is `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace`)\n   - No `output_name`\n\n3. **STEP 3**: Clean the raw catalog using `shell_bash` with:\n   - Command: `cut -d, -f1-3 '<RAW>' > '<WORKSPACE>/earthscope_stations_clean.csv'`\n   - Keep only columns 1-3 (station id and two coordinate columns)\n   - Output to the Active workspace root\n\nThen set `workflow_state.acquisition.metadata_path` to the cleaned workspace path and FINISH.\n\nThe trajectory is currently EMPTY, so I need to start with the first tool call.\n\nLet me start with STEP 1:\n\n**Next Thought**: I need to search for the EarthScope station metadata catalog. Following the exact protocol, I will make the first tool call to search for the \"earthscope converted\" dataset.\n\n**Next Tool Name**: `ndp_search_datasets`\n\n**Next Tool Args**: \n```json\n{\n  \"search_terms\": [\"earthscope\", \"converted\"],\n  \"limit\": 10\n}\n```\n\nThis is STEP 1 of the three-step process."}, "replay": true}

