in ','` reconstructs them as a comma-separated string before writing to disk. The `cut` command won't work in PowerShell since it's a Unix utility. I need to use a PowerShell-native approach instead\u2014splitting each line by comma, selecting the first three fields with array indexing `[0..2]`, and rejoining them. This should extract just the station columns I need from the CSV file. The `cut` command isn't available in Windows PowerShell, so I need to switch to a PowerShell-native approach. I'll use Get-Content to read the CSV file, then pipe each line through ForEach-Object to split by comma and extract the first three columns, joining them back with commas before writing to the output file."}}

