data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:39:57.328456+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_006d965489ed", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this carefully.\n\n## Current State Summary\n\nThe user is asking me (the EarthScope Data Acquisition Expert orchestrator) to:\n1. Discover EarthScope GNSS stations within 50 km of Los Angeles\n2. Rank candidates by distance\n3. Stage and return the time-series CSV path for the nearest station\n\n## Progress So Far\n\nFrom the workflow state provided:\n- **Geospatial resolution**: \u2713 COMPLETE - Los Angeles resolved to bbox and center coordinates\n- **NDP Dataset Discovery**: \u2713 COMPLETE - The EarthScope station metadata catalog has been discovered and staged at:\n  - `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`\n  - Source: `https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv`\n\n**Current workflow_state shows**:\n```json\n{\n  \"acquisition\": {\n    \"analysis_ready\": false,\n    \"metadata_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv\",\n    \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://...\",\n    \"status\": \"metadata_only\"\n  },\n  \"catalog\": {\n    \"status\": \"metadata_found\"\n  },\n  \"geospatial\": {\n    \"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306],\n    \"center_lat\": 34.0536909,\n    \"center_lon\": -118.242766,\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\",\n    \"radius_km\": 50,\n    \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\",\n    \"status\": \"resolved\",\n    \"warnings\": [...]\n  },\n  \"pipeline_stage\": \"data_acquisition_starting\"\n}\n```\n\n## What's Next?\n\nThe workflow requires two remaining steps:\n1. \u2713 `ndp_dataset_discovery` - DONE (metadata_path staged)\n2. \u2192 `earthscope_station_catalog` - NOT YET RUN (needs to rank stations using the metadata)\n3. \u2192 `ndp_timeseries_acquisition` - PENDING (will fetch the nearest station's data)\n\nI need to load the metadata CSV, filter stations within the 50 km radius around Los Angeles center (34.0536909, -118.242766), calculate distances, and identify the closest candidate for time-series retrieval. ` consumes the ranked queries, stages the selected station time-series CSV, and returns `acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, and `acquisition.local_path`.\n\nNow I need to call `earthscope_station_catalog`. It should take the metadata path we have and filter stations within 50 km of LA's center point (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), then rank them by proximity. The task is to process the station metadata CSV at the path we obtained, identify all candidates in that radius, and return them ordered by distance.\n\nI'm delegating to child experts and must pass their outputs verbatim without inventing new data. The geospatial resolution is done, the metadata catalog is staged\u2014now the station ranker needs to run before I can move to the resource resolver stage to get the actual time-series data staged. The next step involves ranking candidates by their distance from the target location, then returning an ordered list. This ranking is essential\u2014`ndp_resource_resolver` needs it to stage the top candidate's time-series CSV data.\n\nI'm passing control to the next child expert now; there's no final answer at this stage. The workflow_state remains unchanged and already includes the metadata_path and resolved geospatial information with the bounding box, center coordinates, high-confidence region name, and default 50 km search radius applied."}}

