data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:43:44.396574+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_9a66c89914c5", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "The station catalog metadata was successfully filtered using the confirmed geospatial parameters (center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W; radius: 50 km).\n\n**Process followed:**\n1. Inspected the CSV file header and sample rows to identify actual column structure, confirming:\n   - Column 1 (Site): station IDs\n   - Column 2 (Latitude): latitude values near 34\u00b0N (range 33\u201334\u00b0)\n   - Column 3 (deg): longitude values near -118\u00b0W (range -117 to -118\u00b0), despite the malformed header name\n2. Resolved UTF-16 encoding issue by converting the catalog to UTF-8\n3. Called `geo_filter_points_by_radius` with explicit column mappings: `lat_column=\"Latitude\"`, `lon_column=\"(deg)\"`, `id_column=\"Site\"`\n4. Tool execution succeeded: `within_radius_count=72`, `skipped_invalid=0`, confirming correct column resolution and valid coordinate parsing across all rows\n\n**Coverage findings:**\n- **72 stations** fall within the 50 km radius (out of 1,101 total in the full catalog)\n- Stations range from **0.3 km** (MTA1, nearly coincident with region center) to **49.6 km** (CLAR, just inside radius)\n- All returned points are sorted ascending by distance_km, providing a ranked candidate set for further resource resolution\n- Network diversity is evident (multiple stations clustered near downtown Los Angeles, with secondary clusters in Long Beach, the San Gabriel Valley, and beyond)\n\n"}}

