iscovery** staged the EarthScope station metadata catalog (`acquisition.metadata_path=D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`).\n2. **\u2713 earthscope_station_catalog** ranked 72 nearby stations by distance to Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), with **MTA1** as the nearest candidate (0.30 km away).\n\nCurrent state:\n- `acquisition.status=metadata_only` (correct\u2014we have the catalog but not yet a concrete station time-series CSV)\n- `acquisition.analysis_ready=false` (correct\u2014no staged CSV yet)\n- `station_catalog.status=ranked` (ready for resolution)\n\n**Critical rule (from system instructions):** \"YOU ARE NOT DONE WHEN THE CATALOG RANKS STATIONS... Your branch is complete ONLY when `ndp_resource_resolver` has staged a real station time-series CSV (`acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, a concrete `acquisition.local_path`), OR the catalog found NO station in radius... Do NOT emit `next_expert=finish` while you have ranked stations but no staged CSV \u2014 that leaves the analysis branch with nothing to plot.\"\n\nI have ranked candidates (72 stations) but no staged CSV. The next and final required step is to invoke `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the time-series data for the top candidate (MTA1) or subsequent candidates from the ranked list, and return a concrete analysis-ready CSV path.", "status": "running", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "data", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "stage": "delegate.started", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "depth": 0, "execution_mode": "blueprint_react"}}}

