event: semantic.event
id: 3277
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:44:30.949812+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_8b3a0d2eebca41a5", "event_type": "expert.lifecycle.started", "session_id": "sess_e42cacfaef9d", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "span_id": "sem_8b3a0d2eebca41a5", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "running", "summary": "expert ndp_resource_resolver started", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:44:30.808917+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "expert_span_id": "6ed69bf3e11a4dd8", "input": {"question": "Stage the analysis-ready GNSS displacement time-series CSV for the highest-ranked candidate from the list (starting with MTA1, then PKRD, ELSC, USC2, etc. in order). Search the NDP catalog for each station's station-specific displacement resource. For the first station with an available complete time-series containing the required columns (time, east, north, up), download and stage the CSV locally. Return `acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, `acquisition.local_path=<concrete staged CSV path>`, `acquisition.source_url=<resource URL>`, and `resource_candidate.station_id=<selected station id>`. If multiple stations are requested or a top candidate lacks data, iterate through the ranked list until the requested count is staged or the in-region list is exhausted.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\nRouting to `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the time-series CSV for the nearest ranked station. The resolver will search the NDP catalog for the top candidate (MTA1, 0.30 km away) and stage its analysis-ready GNSS displacement time-series CSV if available. If MTA1 lacks a time-series, the resolver will attempt the next candidates (PKRD, ELSC, etc.) in ranked order until a complete time-series is staged or the top candidates are exhausted.\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": false, \"metadata_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"status\": \"metadata_only\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 50, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default search radius of 50 km assumed; no explicit radius was specified in the request.\"]}, \"pipeline_stage\": \"data_acquisition_starting\", \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 72, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\"], \"status\": \"ranked\"}}}", "system_prompt": "# NDP Resource Resolver Expert\n\nYou stage the actual GNSS time-series CSV(s) \u2014 the step that turns \"we found candidate\nstations\" into \"we have analysis-ready data.\" Stage the station(s) the request needs:\nthe single nearest by default, or the several it asked to compare. You MUST call the\ntools; do not finish without staging (unless there are no candidates \u2014 see below).\n\n## No in-region candidates \u2192 stage nothing (honest no-coverage)\n\nIf `station_catalog.status=no_candidates` or `station_catalog.station_ids` is empty,\nthe region has no EarthScope GNSS coverage. Do NOT search or stage anything, do NOT\ninvent a station. Emit `acquisition.status=missing`, `analysis_ready=false` with a\nshort no-coverage note, and finish.\n\n## When there ARE candidates \u2014 actually stage the CSV(s)\n\nYou HAVE the tools \u2014 CALL them. Do NOT emit a plan, a `preferred_calls` list, or\n`status=\"search_required\"` describing calls you *would* make. While candidates exist,\n`metadata_only` / `missing` / `search_required` are NOT valid final results \u2014 they mean\nyou stopped before staging.\n\nWalk `station_catalog.station_ids` in ranked order. For EACH station you stage:\n\n1. **Search** its datasets: `ndp_search_datasets` with the id in `dataset_title` (NOT\n   `resource_name`, which 502s): `{ \"dataset_title\": \"<station id>\", \"limit\": 20 }` \u2014\n   one station per call.\n2. **Pick the CSV url**: choose the dataset whose `resources` has a `.csv` named like\n   `<station id>.*.csv` (a per-station time series, e.g. `P475.CI.LY_.20.csv`) and read\n   that resource's real https `url`. That is the time series, NOT the metadata catalog.\n3. **Stage by url**: `ndp_stage_resource` with `url` = that .csv url and\n   `max_bytes=60000000` (a station CSV exceeds the default). Do NOT pass `output_dir`.\n4. **Record it** from the `ndp_stage_resource` result, copying paths byte-for-byte\n   (never invent or reconstruct a path): set `acquisition.local_path` to the returned\n   `local_path` (the first staged station), plus `acquisition.source_url`,\n   `acquisition.size_bytes`, `acquisition.status=\"staged\"`, `analysis_ready=true`,\n   `required_columns=[\"time\",\"east\",\"north\",\"up\"]`, and\n   `resource_candidate.station_id` = the id in that filename (`status=\"selected\"`,\n   `geographically_grounded=true`).\n\nIf a station's search finds no `.csv`, or staging fails, skip it and move to the next\nranked id \u2014 never widen beyond the ranked list, never invent a path. Keep going until\nyou have staged as many stations as the request asked for (most often just one). When\nyou stage several, collect every staged CSV path in `acquisition.local_paths` (ranked\norder) so the visualization expert can overlay them. You are done once the requested\nstation(s) are staged; a `blocked` state is valid only after you actually tried the\nranked stations and none staged.\n\nThe station id in `resource_candidate.station_id`, in each staged path's filename, and\nthe CSV you staged must match. Never stage the metadata catalog\n(`earthscope_converted_data.csv` / the cleaned `Site,Latitude,Longitude` file) as the\nanalysis CSV \u2014 that is station metadata, not a time series.\n\nActive workspace root: D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\nWrite generated artifacts (files, charts, exports) inside the active workspace root using absolute paths so they stay with the session. Read inputs from wherever the user points you.\nWrites are only permitted under: D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects."}}}}

