data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:44:42.813544+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_a359b0239519", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "This is a complex request. Let me break down what's being asked:\n\n1. I'm an Agent expert called `ndp_resource_resolver`\n2. My task is to stage GNSS time-series CSV data for the highest-ranked candidate stations\n3. The ranked station list starts with: MTA1, PKRD, ELSC, USC2, etc.\n4. I have 4 tools available:\n   - `ndp_search_datasets`: Search for datasets in NDP\n   - `ndp_get_dataset_details`: Get detailed metadata for a dataset\n   - `ndp_stage_resource`: Download/stage a resource\n   - `finish`: Mark task complete\n\n5. The current workflow state shows:\n   - `station_catalog.status = \"ranked\"` with 72 candidate stations\n   - First station to try: MTA1\n   - No staged data yet (`acquisition.status = \"metadata_only\"`)\n   - The trajectory is empty (no prior tool calls)\n\nThe instructions are clear:\n1. Search for the dataset using the station id in `dataset_title`\n2. Find the CSV resource with format matching `<station_id>.*.csv`\n3. Get the real https URL from that resource\n4. Stage the resource using `ndp_stage_resource` with `max_bytes=60000000`\n5. Record the results in the specified format\n\nSince the trajectory is empty, I need to make my first tool call. Let me start by searching for the first station: MTA1.\n\nAccording to the instructions:\n- Search with `ndp_search_datasets` using `dataset_title: \"MTA1\"` and `limit: 20`\n- This is one station per call\n- Look for CSV resources named like `MTA1.*.csv`\n\nSo my next thought should explain that I'm starting with the first candidate (MTA1) and searching for its dataset.\n\nMy next tool should be: `ndp_search_datasets`\nI'll query the NDP catalog for datasets matching the top-ranked station MTA1 to locate the GNSS displacement time-series CSV file. The search will use a limit of 20 results to find relevant datasets containing this station's data."}}

