id: 3610
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:45:41.220969+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_26ed5b4992d54d90", "event_type": "blueprint.delegation.completed", "session_id": "sess_e42cacfaef9d", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "span_id": "sem_26ed5b4992d54d90", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "ndp_resource_resolver returned to data.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:45:41.089146+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "role": "child_expert"}, "subject": {"agent_id": "data", "role": "parent_expert"}, "blueprint": {"pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "data", "child_expert": "ndp_resource_resolver"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"delegate_to": "ndp_resource_resolver", "agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "question": "Stage the analysis-ready GNSS displacement time-series CSV for the highest-ranked candidate from the list (starting with MTA1, then PKRD, ELSC, USC2, etc. in order). Search the NDP catalog for each station's station-specific displacement resource. For the first station with an available complete time-series containing the required columns (time, east, north, up), download and stage the CSV locally. Return `acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, `acquisition.local_path=<concrete staged CSV path>`, `acquisition.source_url=<resource URL>`, and `resource_candidate.station_id=<selected station id>`. If multiple stations are requested or a top candidate lacks data, iterate through the ranked list until the requested count is staged or the in-region list is exhausted.", "thought": "The data acquisition pipeline has successfully completed two critical stages:\n\n1. **\u2713 ndp_dataset_discovery** staged the EarthScope station metadata catalog (`acquisition.metadata_path=D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv`).\n2. **\u2713 earthscope_station_catalog** ranked 72 nearby stations by distance to Los Angeles center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), with **MTA1** as the nearest candidate (0.30 km away).\n\nCurrent state:\n- `acquisition.status=metadata_only` (correct\u2014we have the catalog but not yet a concrete station time-series CSV)\n- `acquisition.analysis_ready=false` (correct\u2014no staged CSV yet)\n- `station_catalog.status=ranked` (ready for resolution)\n\n**Critical rule (from system instructions):** \"YOU ARE NOT DONE WHEN THE CATALOG RANKS STATIONS... Your branch is complete ONLY when `ndp_resource_resolver` has staged a real station time-series CSV (`acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, a concrete `acquisition.local_path`), OR the catalog found NO station in radius... Do NOT emit `next_expert=finish` while you have ranked stations but no staged CSV \u2014 that leaves the analysis branch with nothing to plot.\"\n\nI have ranked candidates (72 stations) but no staged CSV. The next and final required step is to invoke `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the time-series data for the top candidate (MTA1) or subsequent candidates from the ranked list, and return a concrete analysis-ready CSV path.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "data", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "data", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 70737, "execution_mode": "blueprint_react", "input": "Stage the analysis-ready GNSS displacement time-series CSV for the highest-ranked candidate from the list (starting with MTA1, then PKRD, ELSC, USC2, etc. in order). Search the NDP catalog for each station's station-specific displacement resource. For the first station with an available complete time-series containing the required columns (time, east, north, up), download and stage the CSV locally. Return `acquisition.status=staged`, `acquisition.analysis_ready=true`, `acquisition.local_path=<concrete staged CSV path>`, `acquisition.source_url=<resource URL>`, and `resource_candidate.station_id=<selected station id>`. If multiple stations are requested or a top candidate lacks data, iterate through the ranked list until the requested count is staged or the in-region list is exhausted.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\nRouting to `ndp_resource_resolver` to stage the time-series CSV for the nearest ranked station. The resolver will search the NDP catalog for the top candidate (MTA1, 0.30 km away) and stage its analysis-ready GNSS displacement time-series CSV if available. If MTA1 lacks a time-series, the resolver will attempt the next candidates (PKRD, ELSC, etc.) in ranked order until a complete time-series is staged or the top candidates are exhausted.\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": false, \"metadata_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"status\": \"metadata_only\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 50, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\