data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:47:19.392787+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_b0df1aec1511", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this carefully.\n\n## Understanding the Request\n\nThe user asked for:\n1. Find the nearest EarthScope GNSS station to Los Angeles\n2. Stage its time-series CSV\n3. Profile it\n4. Create a displacement time-series plot\n\n## Current State\n\nI've received results from two child experts:\n1. **geospatial**: Completed \u2713\n   - Region resolved: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California\n   - Center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n   - Radius: 50 km\n   - Confidence: high\n\n2. **data**: Completed \u2713\n   - 72 stations discovered within 50 km\n   - Selected station: MTA1 (0.30 km away - nearest)\n   - Staged CSV path: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n   - Source URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n   - File size: 50,424,246 bytes\n   - Analysis status: Ready (analysis_ready=true)\n\n## Workflow State Analysis\n\nThe typed workflow_state shows:\n- `acquisition.status`: \"staged\" \u2713\n- `acquisition.analysis_ready`: true \u2713\n- `acquisition.local_path`: The staged CSV path\n- `profile`: \"None\" (not yet done)\n- `visualization`: \"None\" (not yet done)\n\n## Children Not Yet Run\n\nAccording to the prompt:\n- Not yet run: ['analysis', 'synthesis', 'visualization']\n- Already run: ['geospatial', 'data']\n\n## What the User Asked For\n\nThe request requires:\n1. \u2713 Find nearest station \u2192 geospatial + data completed\n2. \u2713 Stage CSV \u2192 data completed, acquisition.status = \"staged\"\n3. \u2717 Profile it \u2192 analysis not run yet\n4. \u2717 Create plot \u2192 visualization not run yet\n\n## Decision Logic\n\nThe system instructions say:\n> Asks to STAGE / explore / inspect a station's dataset \u2192 also take `data` through staging, then `analysis` (profile), then `synthesis`.\n\nAnd for visualization:\n> Asks to PLOT / chart / visualize displacement \u2192 also run `visualization`.\n\nThe user explicitly asked for:\n- \"profile it\" \u2192 needs `analysis`\n- \"create a displacement time-series plot\" \u2192 needs `visualization`\n\nThe instructions also state that when a user asks to profile or visualize data, I should run the corresponding analysis and visualization experts. Since the data is staged and ready, I need to proceed with running `analysis` to generate the profile, then `visualization` to create the displacement time-series plot.\n\nThe staged CSV serves as the trigger to continue downstream processing. With acquisition.status = \"staged\" and analysis_ready = true, I should route to `analysis` first since the visualization likely depends on the profiling results, then move to `visualization` for the plot.\n\nThe user explicitly requested both profiling and a displacement time-series plot. Analysis needs to profile the GNSS time-series CSV at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` and produce workflow_state.profile, which will inform the subsequent visualization step. The nearest EarthScope GNSS station has been identified and its CSV staged at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`. Now I need to profile this data to understand the displacement time-series characteristics before visualization. I'll route to the analysis expert to examine the station's suitability, assess data quality metrics like temporal coverage and missing values, and compute statistics across the east, north, and up displacement components. I need to complete the partial thought from the current rewritten thinking first.\n\nThe current rewritten thinking ends mid-sentence with \"for plot)\" - this is incomplete. I need to copy from the next thinking to finish this thought properly.\n\nLooking at the next thinking, I can see it continues with \"- synthesis: \u2717 not run (always run last)\" which completes the list that was being cut off.\n\nHere's the completed and rewritten thinking:\n\nThe instructions are clear: I shouldn't finish until the workflow is complete, every claim has evidence backing it, and synthesis has produced a final brief. Right now I'm missing the profiling analysis the user requested and the visualization they asked for, so I need to keep delegating. Geospatial and data preparation are done, but analysis hasn't run yet, visualization hasn't run, and synthesis is still pending. My next move is to route to analysis to profile that staged CSV, then visualization for the plot, and finally synthesis before completing the task."}}

