ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n   - This is my FIRST and ONLY tool call for this step\n   - I should NOT invent any paths or filenames\n   - I should NOT reason about or transform the path\n\n6. **Output format required**:\n   - `next_thought` (str)\n   - `next_tool_name` (must be exactly `pandas_profile_csv`)\n   - `next_tool_input` with `data_path` parameter set to the staged file path\n\nThe staged GNSS file is ready at `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv` (50424246 bytes, status confirmed as \"staged\"). I'll invoke pandas_profile_csv on this exact path to analyze the dataset structure\u2014row count, column names, data types, value ranges for the GNSS coordinates (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU), and any missing data patterns.\n\n**next_tool_name**: `pandas_profile_csv`\n\n**next_tool_args**: \n```json\n{\n  \"data_path\": \"D:\\\\Libraries\\\\Documents\\\\projects\\\\ndp-demo-workspace\\\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\"\n}\n```\n\nI'm leaving `columns` and `max_rows` unspecified to get a full profile of all available columns and use the default sampling behavior. This gives me complete visibility into what the dataset contains without artificially restricting the analysis.\n\nFor the file path, I need to ensure proper JSON encoding\u2014the double backslashes in the workflow state represent single backslashes in the actual path string, which is the correct format for the tool argument."}}

