data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:48:41.372569+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_92a911bfc1d9", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "Let me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe user is asking me to profile a GNSS time-series CSV file. The workflow state shows:\n1. The staged CSV path is: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n2. The file size is 50424246 bytes\n3. This is for station MTA1\n\nThe first thought (thought_0) and tool call (tool_name_0 and tool_args_0) have already been executed in the trajectory, and I have an observation back (observation_0).\n\nThe observation shows:\n- Successfully profiled the file\n- 8 columns present: time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel\n- Row count: 250000 total rows\n- Rows profiled: 5000 (out of a row_scan_cap of 250000)\n- The profiling was scan_limited and profile_limited\n- No null values found\n- Numeric summaries provided for all columns\n- Time range: 1733184000000.0 to 1733189070000.0 (in milliseconds, appears to be Unix timestamp milliseconds)\n- Displacement columns (east, north, up) have numeric ranges\n- Uncertainty columns (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU) have numeric ranges\n- Sample rows show time delta of 1000ms (1 second) between consecutive rows\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Evaluate the profiling results\n2. Prepare the final output with workflow_state containing the profile information\n3. Mark the task as complete using the `finish` tool\n\nThe instruction says:\n- Return row count scanned/examined, rows actually profiled for numeric summaries\n- File size, columns present\n- Numeric min/max/mean ranges for displacement and uncertainty columns\n- Missing-column caveats\n- Whether analysis used sampled profile\n- Treat `numeric_summary_rows` as scope of min/max/mean statistics\n- Never convert rows_scanned into duration/cadence/sampling rate\n- Only say visible sample rows suggest spacing, don't generalize\n- Don't infer full-file properties from partial scan\n- Report findings in workflow_state.profile with status and caveats\n\nThe profiling succeeded and I have the necessary data. I should now formulate a summary acknowledging the successful profile scan of the staged file, note that results are based on a 5000-row sample from the full 250000-row dataset, and prepare to finalize with the finish tool. The finish tool requires an empty dict for arguments, but I need to ensure the profiling results are captured in the workflow_state before completing. Looking at the output schema, the workflow_state should include the acquisition status with the staged CSV path, plus a profile section documenting the scan results, column information, and any limitations encountered. I'll synthesize the profiling findings in my next_thought to make sure all this data is available when the finish call executes. iled_rows only, not full 250000-row file\", \"Sampling cadence inferred from sample rows only (1000ms delta visible); not verified across full file\", \"Time range shown is for 5000 profiled rows only\"]. The timestamps convert to December 3, 2024, spanning roughly 1 hour 24 minutes across the profiled subset.\n\nNow I can format the response with the workflow state and indicate the next step."}}

