\n- qChannel column: present (integer); range 1,314,021\u20132,411,021 in profiled rows. Treated as opaque metadata; no quality interpretation applied.\n\n**Profile Limitations & Caveats**\n1. Numeric min/max/mean statistics are computed on 5,000 profiled rows only; do not generalize to full 250,000-row file.\n2. Time range and observed cadence are descriptive of the profiled sample; full-file duration, complete time span, and cadence verification are beyond this profile scope.\n3. Missing-value counts are scoped to profiled rows only; no full-file gap analysis performed.\n4. No noise assessment, continuity checks, or data quality thresholds applied.\n5. Profile is scan-limited and profile-limited by design; partial profiling used for efficiency.\n6. qChannel values are metadata flags; no decoding or quality rating supplied.\n\n**Conclusion**\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS CSV is ready for downstream analysis. All required displacement and uncertainty columns are present with numeric data intact in the profiled sample. Time bounds, cadence, and numeric ranges are documented for the profiled rows with explicit caveats about scan-limited scope."}}}

