id: 5194
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:51:33.213959+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_24db735afee54066", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_e42cacfaef9d", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "span_id": "sem_24db735afee54066", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert station_network_analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:51:33.070738+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "station_network_analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "analysis"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "station_network_analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'station_network_analysis'.", "answer": "**Station MTA1 Suitability Assessment (Preliminary, Scan-Limited)**\n\n**Data Structure**: MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv contains all 8 required columns (time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel) for GNSS displacement analysis.\n\n**Uncertainty Levels (Profiled Sample)**:\n- Horizontal uncertainty (sigEE/sigNN): ~0.033 m mean (3.3 cm)\n- Vertical uncertainty (sigUU): ~0.065 m mean (6.5 cm)\n- Uncertainty values represent centimeter-scale precision appropriate for horizontal displacement work; vertical uncertainty is approximately twice horizontal, consistent with typical GNSS characteristics.\n\n**Missing Values**: 0 detected in 5,000 profiled rows; full-file missing-value status not assessed.\n\n**Cadence Observation**: ~1,000 ms observed in profiled sample; full-file cadence not verified.\n\n**Preliminary Suitability Status**: MTA1 is structurally and geographically grounded as a displacement analysis candidate. Required columns are complete, profiled-row uncertainties fall within displacement-monitoring ranges (centimeter-scale horizontal, decimeter-scale vertical), and no missing values were detected in the profiled sample.\n\n**Critical Limitations**:\n- Profile is scan-limited: 5,000 rows profiled of 250,000 total rows\n- Full-file time range, cadence, continuity, and gap characteristics remain unverified\n- Profiled time span (~5,070 s) may not represent full-file duration\n- qChannel metadata present but not decoded; no quality threshold interpretation available\n- Full-file statistics (cadence, duration, completeness, noise) required before confirming suitability for production displacement analysis\n\n**Recommendation**: MTA1 merits full-file verification (complete-scan profiling, gap analysis, time-range confirmation). Parallel consideration of network redundancy from the 72-station Los Angeles catalog is recommended to cross-validate results and mitigate single-station risk.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "MTA1 profiling has provided structural and uncertainty evidence at scan-limited scope. The assessment must balance what has been verified (column presence, profiled-row uncertainty ranges, profiled-row missing values, observed cadence in profiled sample) against what remains unverified (full-file cadence, full-file duration, full-file gap analysis, qChannel decoding). \n\nColumn completeness confirms the required displacement fields are present. Uncertainty levels in the profiled 5,000-row sample\u2014horizontal ~0.033 m (3.3 cm) and vertical ~0.065 m (6.5 cm)\u2014fall within typical centimeter-scale GNSS uncertainty ranges suitable for displacement monitoring. Zero missing values in profiled rows is a positive indicator. However, the profiler scanned only 5,000 of 250,000 rows; cadence (~1,000 ms), time span (~5,070 s), and gap behavior cannot be generalized to the full file without complete-file analysis. qChannel flags are present but not decoded, so no quality rating can be inferred from them. Geographic grounding in the Los Angeles region is confirmed by the metadata catalog and geospatial workflow state.\n\nSuitability is preliminary and geographically grounded, but full-file verification is required before confirming readiness for rigorous displacement analysis."}}}

