event: message.part.completed
id: 5197
data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:51:34.002589+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_a9f03a928a33", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "MTA1 profiling has provided structural and uncertainty evidence at scan-limited scope. The assessment must balance what has been verified (column presence, profiled-row uncertainty ranges, profiled-row missing values, observed cadence in profiled sample) against what remains unverified (full-file cadence, full-file duration, full-file gap analysis, qChannel decoding).\n\nColumn completeness confirms the required displacement fields are present. Uncertainty levels in the profiled 5,000-row sample\u2014horizontal ~0.033 m (3.3 cm) and vertical ~0.065 m (6.5 cm)\u2014fall within typical centimeter-scale GNSS uncertainty ranges suitable for displacement monitoring. Zero missing values in profiled rows is a positive indicator. However, the profiler scanned only 5,000 of 250,000 rows; cadence (~1,000 ms), time span (~5,070 s), and gap behavior cannot be generalized to the full file without complete-file analysis. qChannel flags are present but not decoded, so no quality rating can be inferred from them. Geographic grounding in the Los Angeles region is confirmed by the metadata catalog anSuitability is preliminary and geographically grounded, but full-file verification is required before confirming readiness for rigorous displacement analysis.\n\n"}}

