id: 5525
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:52:50.288881+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_c9a659ccb8c2460e", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_e42cacfaef9d", "workspace_id": "ws_ndp_demo", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "span_id": "sem_c9a659ccb8c2460e", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:52:50.151960+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'analysis'.", "answer": "# GNSS Time-Series Profile & Station Suitability Summary \u2014 MTA1\n\n## Staged Data\n- **File**: `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Size**: 50,424,246 bytes\n- **Rows in file**: 250,000 total\n- **Rows profiled (numeric summaries)**: 5,000\n- **Source URL**: https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\n\n## Structure\n- **Required columns**: All 8 present \u2014 time, east, north, up, sigEE, sigNN, sigUU, qChannel \u2713\n\n## Displacement Components (Profiled Sample, 5,000 rows)\n\n| Component | Min (m)  | Max (m)  | Mean (m) |\n|-----------|----------|----------|----------|\n| East      | \u22120.070   | \u22120.030   | \u22120.0472  |\n| North     | 0.029    | 0.058    | 0.0451   |\n| Up        | 0.051    | 0.224    | 0.1358   |\n\n## Displacement Uncertainty (Profiled Sample, 5,000 rows)\n\n| Uncertainty | Min (m) | Max (m) | Mean (m) |\n|-------------|---------|---------|----------|\n| sigEE (E\u2013W) | 0.032   | 0.035   | 0.0334   |\n| sigNN (N\u2013S) | 0.032   | 0.036   | 0.0330   |\n| sigUU (Vert)| 0.062   | 0.066   | 0.0651   |\n\n## Time Coverage & Cadence (Profiled Sample)\n- **Time range**: 1,733,184,000,000 to 1,733,189,070,000 milliseconds (Unix epoch)\n- **Profiled time span**: ~5,070 seconds (~1 hour 24 minutes)\n- **Observed cadence**: ~1,000 ms between adjacent samples\n- **Caveat**: Full-file time range, complete duration, and cadence verification remain unperformed.\n\n## Data Completeness\n- **Missing values in profiled rows**: 0\n- **Caveat**: Missing-value assessment applies to profiled rows only; full-file gap analysis not performed.\n\n## Station Suitability (Preliminary, Scan-Limited)\n- **Structure**: All required columns intact in profiled sample \u2713\n- **Uncertainty scale**: Horizontal (~0.033 m) and vertical (~0.065 m) uncertainty values span centimeter-to-decimeter range, consistent with typical GNSS instrument precision.\n- **Geospatial context**: Station MTA1 is one of 72 candidates in Los Angeles area network (bbox: \u2212118.67\u00b0 to \u2212118.16\u00b0W, 33.66\u00b0 to 34.34\u00b0N).\n- **Preliminary status**: Structurally sound; suitable for preliminary analysis pending full-file verification.\n\n## Critical Limitations\n\n1. **Statistics scope**: Min/max/mean values are from 5,000 profiled rows only; do not generalize to the full 250,000-row file.\n2. **Time and cadence**: Time range and observed cadence describe the profiled sample; full-file duration and complete-scan cadence verification remain unverified.\n3. **Missing-value assessment**: Counts apply to profiled rows only; no full-file continuity or gap-pattern analysis performed.\n4. **Quality flags**: qChannel metadata is present but not decoded; no quality-threshold interpretation supplied.\n5. **Noise and continuity**: No per-epoch noise assessment, data continuity checks, or quality thresholds applied.\n6. **Partial profiling**: Profile is scan-limited and partial by design; full-file statistical confirmation is needed before production-grade analysis.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMTA1 data structure and sampled statistics support displacement work. However, full-file profiling (cadence verification, gap analysis, complete time-range confirmation, and continuity checks) is required to confirm suitability for production analysis. Parallel evaluation of network redundancy across the 72-station Los Angeles catalog is recommended to validate results and mitigate single-station risk.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "Both required child experts have completed their delegated work:\n\n1. **`gnss_timeseries_analysis`** (completed): Profiled the staged CSV, providing row count (250,000 total, 5,000 profiled), column structure (all 8 required columns present), displacement statistics (east, north, up ranges and means from profiled sample), uncertainty levels (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU), time bounds, observed cadence (~1,000 ms in sample), and explicit caveats about scan-limited profiling scope.\n\n2. **`station_network_analysis`** (completed): Assessed MTA1 suitability based on the profiled evidence, confirming structural completeness, uncertainty scale appropriate for displacement monitoring, zero missing values in profiled rows (with scope caveat), and stating suitability is \"structurally sound pending full-file verification.\" Documented critical limitations about scan-limited profiling.\n\nThe original user request explicitly asked for profiling, displacement analysis, and suitability assessment\u2014all now delivered. The request did **not** ask for earthquake/event catalog analysis. Per workflow rules, the `seismic_event_catalog` child is optional and not required here; no prior tool evidence indicates seismic event context is needed for this GNSS profiling task.\n\nThe profiling and suitability assessment are complete and properly caveated. The task is ready to return to the parent. All claims in the final answer are grounded in the children's typed results and the workflow_state."}}}

