assessment applies to profiled rows only; full-file gap analysis not performed.\n\n## Station Suitability (Preliminary, Scan-Limited)\n- **Structure**: All required columns intact in profiled sample \u2713\n- **Uncertainty scale**: Horizontal (~0.033 m) and vertical (~0.065 m) uncertainty values span centimeter-to-decimeter range, consistent with typical GNSS instrument precision.\n- **Geospatial context**: Station MTA1 is one of 72 candidates in Los Angeles area network (bbox: \u2212118.67\u00b0 to \u2212118.16\u00b0W, 33.66\u00b0 to 34.34\u00b0N).\n- **Preliminary status**: Structurally sound; suitable for preliminary analysis pending full-file verification.\n\n## Critical Limitations\n\n1. **Statistics scope**: Min/max/mean values are from 5,000 profiled rows only; do not generalize to the full 250,000-row file.\n2. **Time and cadence**: Time range and observed cadence describe the profiled sample; full-file duration and complete-scan cadence verification remain unverified.\n3. **Missing-value assessment**: Counts apply to profiled rows only; no full-file continuity or gap-pattern analysis performed.\n4. **Quality flags**: qChannel metadata is present but not decoded; no quality-threshold interpretation supplied.\n5. **Noise and continuity**: No per-epoch noise assessment, data continuity checks, or quality thresholds applied.\n6. **Partial profiling**: Profile is scan-limited and partial by design; full-file statistical confirmation is needed before production-grade analysis.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMTA1 data structure and sampled statistics support displacement work. However, full-file profiling (cadence verification, gap analysis, complete time-range confirmation, and continuity checks) is required to confirm suitability for production analysis. Parallel evaluation of network redundancy across the 72-station Los Angeles catalog is recommended to validate results and mitigate single-station risk.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at