ation_discovery`, `data_staged`, `profile_complete`, `artifact_ready`, and `ready_for_final_answer`. However, the detailed upstream `workflow_state` structure containing the authoritative grounded values is not present in the input provided to me.\n\nSpecifically, I lack the actual values that must be copied verbatim per the core rules:\n- `resource_candidate.station_id` (the leading token from the CSV filename)\n- `acquisition.local_path` (the exact staged CSV path)\n- `acquisition.source_url` (the exact source URL)\n- `artifact.path` (the exact PNG visualization path)\n- `profile.rows_scanned` (the actual count)\n\nThe question prose describes what these values *should* be (MTA1, 5,000 rows, etc.), but the prose is specification/intent, not the authoritative upstream workflow_state. Per the core rule: *\"Every station id, path, URL, and number already exists verbatim in upstream workflow_state/child evidence \u2014 COPY it, never compose/infer/remember. If a value isn't there character-for-character it is a fabrication.\"*\n\nSince the detailed upstream workflow_state was not provided, I cannot construct a grounded answer without violating the data integrity rules."}}}

