data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-30T19:57:10.229529+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_67de8abd5b15", "message_id": "msg_asst_3bad04dabf97", "part_id": "part_6a82b2c87e6c", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "**EarthScope GNSS Analysis Complete \u2014 Los Angeles Region**\n\nYour request to find, stage, profile, and visualize the nearest GNSS station to Los Angeles has been successfully completed.\n\n**Region & Station:**\n- **Location:** Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States (34.0536909\u00b0N, \u2212118.242766\u00b0W, 50 km radius)\n- **Selected Station:** MTA1 \u2014 nearest candidate at 0.30 km distance (72 total candidates ranked)\n- **Provenance:** Geocoded via OSM Nominatim; stations ranked by distance\n\n**Staged Data:**\n- **Local path:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Source URL:** `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **File size:** 50.4 MB | **Total rows:** 250,000 | **Status:** Analysis-ready\n\n**Profile Summary (Scan-Limited, 5,000-Row Sample):**\n\n*Displacement Components (meters):*\n| Component | Min | Max | Mean |\n|-----------|-------|-------|---------|\n| East | \u22120.070 | \u22120.030 | \u22120.047 |\n| North | 0.029 | 0.058 | 0.045 |\n| Up | 0.051 | 0.224 | 0.136 |\n\n*Horizontal & Vertical Uncertainties (1\u03c3, meters):*\n| Uncertainty | Min | Max | Mean |\n|-------------|-------|-------|--------|\n| \u03c3_East | 0.032 | 0.035 | 0.033 |\n| \u03c3_North | 0.032 | 0.036 | 0.033 |\n| \u03c3_Up | 0.062 | 0.066 | 0.065 |\n\n*Time Coverage (Profiled Span):*\n- **Epoch range:** 1733184000000\u20131733189070000 ms (Unix)\n- **Duration:** ~5,070 seconds (\u22481 hour 24 minutes)\n- **Observed cadence:** 1,000 ms | **Missing values:** 0 (in profiled sample)\n\n**Visualization Artifact:**\n- **Path:** `D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\ndp-demo-workspace\\MTA1_displacement.png`\n- **Content:** Three-component displacement time-series (east, north, up) with legends\n- **Rows plotted:** 2,000 (leading rows) | **Cadence shown:** 1,000 ms | **Span:** 1h 24m\n\n**Critical Limitations:**\n- **Profile scope:** Statistics from 5,000 profiled rows only; full-file min/max/mean unverified\n- **Full-file duration & cadence:** Time range describes profiled sample; continuous duration, complete cadence, and gap analysis remain unperformed\n- **Missing-value assessment:** Zero missing values in profiled rows only; full-file continuity not verified\n- **Plot coverage:** First 2,000 rows visualized; long-term trends across all 250,000 rows not shown\n- **Quality metadata:** qChannel flag values present but not decoded\n- **Verification pending:** Full-file statistical confirmation, complete gap analysis, and continuity verification required before production-grade analysis\n\n**Recommendation:**\nMTA1 data structure and sampled statistics support preliminary displacement studies. Full-file profiling (gap detection, complete time-range verification, cadence confirmation) and evaluation of network redundancy across the 72-station Los Angeles catalog recommended for production use."}, "replay": true}

